IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cp6-provinces-and-consent`
IMPORT `cp6-rates-review`

-- Tests of cp6-rates-review.l4 (section 113.1). Every rate below is worked by hand from the formulas of subsections (11.06) to (11.14);
-- the working is in the comment beside it. A rate is written as a percentage: 4.95% is 0.0495.

§ `Tests -- the financial review and the movement of the rates`

§§ `Subsections (1) to (4): the three-year periods`

-- Periods begin in 1998 and every third year after (fork C6-F18).
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 1998 EQUALS JUST 1998
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 1999 EQUALS JUST 1998
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 2000 EQUALS JUST 1998
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 2001 EQUALS JUST 2001
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 2025 EQUALS JUST 2025
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 2027 EQUALS JUST 2025
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 2028 EQUALS JUST 2028
-- Not covered: "once every three years after 1997" requires no review before 1998.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` 1997 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the ministers must review the financial state of the Plan in the three-year period that contains the year` 1998
#ASSERT `s 113.1(1) — the ministers must review the financial state of the Plan in the three-year period that contains the year` 2030
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(1) — the ministers must review the financial state of the Plan in the three-year period that contains the year` 1997)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(2) — the ministers must as part of their review also review the adjustment factors fixed under subsection 46(7)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(2) — the ministers must as part of their review also review the adjustment factors fixed under subsection 46(7)` FALSE)
-- The period 2025 to 2027: its second year ends on 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(3) — the end of the second year of the three-year period, before which the Minister of Finance should be able to make recommendations` 2025 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `the most recent report of the Chief Actuary under section 115 and changes since earlier reports`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `more recent estimates of the Chief Actuary of the account balances, projected revenues and payments, projected asset ratios and changes since the previous review`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `the financing objective for the base Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `the financing objective for the additional Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `that changes that increase benefits or add new benefits must be accompanied by contribution rate increases`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` `another matter`)

§§ `Subsection (5): recommendations`

-- Inputs: a review has been completed; the recommendations include a change.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(5) — the Minister of Finance may recommend to the Governor in Council that regulations be made under subsection 113.1(6)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(5) — the Minister of Finance may recommend to the Governor in Council that regulations be made under subsection 113.1(6)` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(5) — the Minister of Finance may recommend to the Governor in Council that regulations be made under subsection 113.1(6)` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(5) — the Minister of Finance must cause the recommendations to be published in the Canada Gazette` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(5) — the Minister of Finance must cause the recommendations to be published in the Canada Gazette` FALSE)

§§ `Subsection (7): limits on the changes to the rates`

-- (a) and (b): employees and employers identical; self-employed the sum.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` (5.05%) (5.05%) (10.1%)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` (4.95%) (5.0%) (9.95%))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.8%))
-- (c): an increase of exactly one-tenth of a percentage point is allowed, a little more is not, and a decrease is allowed.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(c) — the rate for employees or employers is not increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point` (5.05%) (4.95%)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7)(c) — the rate for employees or employers is not increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point` (5.051%) (4.95%))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(c) — the rate for employees or employers is not increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point` (4.9%) (4.95%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(c) — the rate for employees or employers is not increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point` (4.95%) (4.95%)
-- (d): two-tenths for the self-employed.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7)(d) — the rate for self-employed persons is not increased by more than two-tenths of a percentage point` (10.1%) (9.9%)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7)(d) — the rate for self-employed persons is not increased by more than two-tenths of a percentage point` (10.101%) (9.9%))
-- All limbs together. Inputs: employees, employers, self-employed for the year; then the same for the previous year.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7) — the setting of the rates for the year is within the limits` (5.05%) (5.05%) (10.1%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(7) — the setting of the rates for the year is within the limits` (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%)
-- Employees and employers up by 0.15 of a point: too much.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7) — the setting of the rates for the year is within the limits` (5.1%) (5.1%) (10.2%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%))
-- Employees and employers up by 0.1 but the self-employed rate not the sum.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(7) — the setting of the rates for the year is within the limits` (5.05%) (5.05%) (10.0%) (4.95%) (4.95%) (9.9%))

§§ `Subsections (8), (8.1) and (10): coming into force`

-- The period 2025 to 2027: its third year is 2027, so October 1 is 1 October 2027; the regulation comes into force on 1 January 2028.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(8) — the day the regulation comes into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(8) — the day the regulation comes into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 1 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)
-- Not covered: made on or after October 1 of the third year.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(8) — the day the regulation comes into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 10 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 113.1(8) — the day the regulation comes into force` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2028 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Inputs: the first year of the period; the day the last consent needed was signified; the number of included provinces; the number consenting; the population of all; the population of those consenting.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(8.1) — an order under subsection 113.1(8) may be made` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) 9 6 30000000 20000000
-- The consent came on October 1 itself: not "before" it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(8.1) — an order under subsection 113.1(8) may be made` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 10 1) 9 6 30000000 20000000)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(8.1) — an order under subsection 113.1(8) may be made` 2025 (YearMonthDay 2027 9 30) 9 5 30000000 29000000)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(10) — the Minister of Finance must forthwith cause a copy of the regulation to be published in the Canada Gazette` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(10) — the Minister of Finance must forthwith cause a copy of the regulation to be published in the Canada Gazette` FALSE)

§§ `Subsection (11.06): A, B, C and D`

-- A is half of the rate under 115(1.1)(c)(i): half of 9.0% is 4.5%. C is half of the rate under (c)(ii): half of 0.6% is 0.3%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.06) — A` (9.0%) EQUALS (4.5%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.06) — C` (0.6%) EQUALS (0.3%)
-- D is B less C: 4.4% less 0.3% is 4.1%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.06) — D` (4.4%) (0.6%) EQUALS (4.1%)

§§ `Subsection (11.05): when the rates are insufficient`

-- Inputs: the self-employed rate for the years in the period; the rate under (c)(ii); the rate under (c)(i).
-- 8.8% less 0.6% is 8.2%, which is less than 8.4%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` (8.8%) (0.6%) (8.4%)
-- 9.9% less nothing is 9.9%, which is not less than 9.9%.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` (9.9%) (0%) (9.9%))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` (9.9%) (0%) (9.8%))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` (9.9%) (0%) (9.901%)

-- (11.13): a recommendation to increase that was carried out, or a recommendation not to increase that was published.
-- Inputs: (a) recommended increase; (a) rates increased in time; (b) recommended no increase; (b) published in time.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05) — Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05) — Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05) — Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` TRUE TRUE)
-- The period 2025 to 2027: October 1 of the year before is 1 October 2024; Schedule 1 is deemed amended the next day.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05)(b) — the day Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` 2025 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 10 2
-- (11.05)(a) and (11.12): the benefits ratios are taken as 1 unless the first case applies.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05)(a) and (11.12) — the benefits are determined as if the ratios were each 1` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05)(a) and (11.12) — the benefits are determined as if the ratios were each 1` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.05)(a) and (11.12) — the benefits are determined as if the ratios were each 1` FALSE FALSE)
-- (b)(ii): twice the employers' rate.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.05)(b)(ii) — the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` (4.5%) EQUALS (9.0%)

§§ `Subsections (11.07) to (11.11): which case, and the rate in each`

-- Inputs: the rate under 115(1.1)(c)(i); the rate under (c)(ii); B.
-- First case: 8.4% gives A = 4.2%; 0.6% gives C = 0.3%; B = 4.4% gives D = 4.1%. Neither A nor D is above 4.95% and A is above D.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (8.4%) (0.6%) (4.4%) EQUALS `the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)`
-- The rate is A plus C = 4.5% in every year.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (8.4%) (0.6%) (4.4%) 1 EQUALS JUST (4.5%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (8.4%) (0.6%) (4.4%) 2 EQUALS JUST (4.5%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (8.4%) (0.6%) (4.4%) 3 EQUALS JUST (4.5%)
-- Second case: 10.0% gives A = 5.0%; nothing gives C = 0; B = 4.9% gives D = 4.9%. A is above 4.95%, D is not, and half of (A - D) is 0.05%, at most 0.1%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (10.0%) (0%) (4.9%) EQUALS `the second case, subsection 113.1(11.08)`
-- 4.95% + half of (5.0% - 4.95%) + 0 = 4.95% + 0.025% = 4.975%, in every year.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.0%) (0%) (4.9%) 1 EQUALS JUST (4.975%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.0%) (0%) (4.9%) 5 EQUALS JUST (4.975%)
-- Third case: 10.4% gives A = 5.2%; D = 4.9%; half of (5.2% - 4.9%) is 0.15%, above 0.1%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) EQUALS `the third case, subsection 113.1(11.09)`
-- Year 1: 4.95% + 1/6 of (5.2% - 4.95%) = 4.95% + 0.25%/6; year 2: 4.95% + 0.25%/3; year 3 and after: 4.95% + 0.125% = 5.075%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 1 EQUALS JUST (0.0495 PLUS (0.0025 DIVIDED BY 6))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 2 EQUALS JUST (0.0495 PLUS (0.0025 DIVIDED BY 3))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 3 EQUALS JUST (5.075%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 4 EQUALS JUST (5.075%)
-- Fourth case: 10.0% gives A = 5.0%; B = 5.0% gives D = 5.0%. A and D are both above 4.95%, so cases 2 and 3 do not apply; half of (A - D) is 0.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (10.0%) (0%) (5.0%) EQUALS `the fourth case, subsection 113.1(11.1)`
-- D + half of (A - D) + C = 5.0% + 0 + 0.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (10.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 1 EQUALS JUST (5.0%)
-- Fourth case again, with A below D: 8.0% gives A = 4.0%; B = 4.5% gives D = 4.5%. Half of (4.0% - 4.5%) is minus 0.25%, at most 0.1%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (8.0%) (0%) (4.5%) EQUALS `the fourth case, subsection 113.1(11.1)`
-- 4.5% + half of (4.0% - 4.5%) = 4.5% - 0.25% = 4.25%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (8.0%) (0%) (4.5%) 1 EQUALS JUST (4.25%)
-- Fifth case: 11.0% gives A = 5.5%; B = 5.0% gives D = 5.0%; half of (5.5% - 5.0%) is 0.25%, above 0.1%; D is above 4.95% so cases 2 and 3 do not apply.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) EQUALS `the fifth case, subsection 113.1(11.11)`
-- Year 1: 5.0% + 1/6 of 0.5%; year 2: 5.0% + 1/3 of 0.5%; year 3 and after: 5.0% + 0.25% = 5.25%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 1 EQUALS JUST (0.05 PLUS (0.005 DIVIDED BY 6))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 2 EQUALS JUST (0.05 PLUS (0.005 DIVIDED BY 3))
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 3 EQUALS JUST (5.25%)
-- Not covered: there is no year before the first.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` (8.4%) (0.6%) (4.4%) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection (11.14): rounding to the nearest multiple of 0.005%`

-- Already a multiple.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (4.95%) EQUALS (4.95%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (4.975%) EQUALS (4.975%)
-- 4.99166...% is 998.33 multiples: down to 998, which is 4.99%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (0.0495 PLUS (0.0025 DIVIDED BY 6)) EQUALS (4.99%)
-- 5.03333...% is 1006.67 multiples: up to 1007, which is 5.035%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (0.0495 PLUS (0.0025 DIVIDED BY 3)) EQUALS (5.035%)
-- Exactly halfway rounds up (fork C6-F19): 5.0025% is 1000.5 multiples, so 1001, which is 5.005%; a hair below is 5.000%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (5.0025%) EQUALS (5.005%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (5.00249%) EQUALS (5.0%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` (4.9975%) EQUALS (5.0%)
-- The 5th-case rates: 5.08333...% is 1016.67 multiples, up to 5.085%; 5.16666...% is 1033.33, down to 5.165%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 1 EQUALS JUST (5.085%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 2 EQUALS JUST (5.165%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (11.0%) (0%) (5.0%) 3 EQUALS JUST (5.25%)
-- The 3rd-case rates: 4.99%, 5.035%, 5.075%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 1 EQUALS JUST (4.99%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 2 EQUALS JUST (5.035%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 3 EQUALS JUST (5.075%)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` (10.4%) (0%) (4.9%) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsections (11.141) to (11.146): the additional Canada Pension Plan`

-- Inputs: the four conditions of paragraphs (a) to (d), each as "within a range set out in the regulations".
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The difference of paragraph (a): 2.0% in Schedule 2 less 1.9% in the report is 0.1%.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — the difference between the Schedule 2 rate and the rate in the most recent report` (2.0%) (1.9%) EQUALS (0.1%)
-- Inputs: (a) recommended a change; changed in time; (b) recommended no change; published in time.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.143) — subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.143) — subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.143) — subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.143) — subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — Schedule 2 is deemed to have been amended` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.141) — Schedule 2 is deemed to have been amended` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.141) — Schedule 2 is deemed to have been amended` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.142) — the portions of benefits in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan are determined in accordance with the regulations` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.142) — the portions of benefits in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan are determined in accordance with the regulations` TRUE TRUE)
-- Not covered: the calculations are in regulations that are not deposited.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.141) — the first or second additional contribution rate for a year after a deemed amendment` 2028 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.145) — regulations under subsection 113.1(11.144) may be made` 9 6 30000000 20000000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.145) — regulations under subsection 113.1(11.144) may be made` 9 5 30000000 20000000)
-- The first review after 2027 is the one for the period beginning in 2028; then every third review: 2037, 2046.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2028
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2037
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2046
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2031)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.146) — the ministers must also review the regulations in the review of the three-year period` 2034)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(11.15) — the Minister of Finance must publish the amendment in the Canada Gazette` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(11.15) — the Minister of Finance must publish the amendment in the Canada Gazette` FALSE)

§§ `Subsections (13) to (16)`

#ASSERT `s 113.1(13) — the Minister of Finance may recommend to the Governor in Council that the regulations made under subsection 46(7) be amended` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(13) — the Minister of Finance may recommend to the Governor in Council that the regulations made under subsection 46(7) be amended` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(13) — the Minister of Finance must cause the recommendations to be published in the Canada Gazette` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(13) — the Minister of Finance must cause the recommendations to be published in the Canada Gazette` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 113.1(15) — the regulations on the adjustment factors may be amended` 9 6 30000000 20000000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(15) — the regulations on the adjustment factors may be amended` 9 6 30000000 19999999)

`cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Test province B"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

`cp6 test Nunavut` MEANS Province WITH
    `name of the province` IS "Nunavut"
    `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS FALSE

-- Subsection (16): "included province" is section 114(1)'s.
#ASSERT `s 113.1(16) — a province is an included province for section 113.1` `cp6 test province not providing a comprehensive pension plan` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 113.1(16) — a province is an included province for section 113.1` `cp6 test Nunavut` FALSE)
